# Copy to .env (gitignored) or export these in the environment.

# Independent CommandCode API key for this project. Required for the filter to run.
# Create it in the CommandCode Studio (Settings -> API keys); never commit or paste it.
commandcode_apikey=

# Optional: linux.do session cookie. Only needed if topic-detail fetches start
# getting Cloudflare-challenged on your network. The list endpoint works without it.
# linuxdo_cookie=

# Optional: allow falling back to the Hermes credential pool (~/.hermes/auth.json)
# when no key is set above. Dev only.
# LINUXDO_AI_ALLOW_POOL_KEY=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- owner boundary
# The owner token authorises the writes (POST /api/queue, /api/feedback, /api/refresh) and
# the owner-only reads (GET /api/feedback, GET /api/failures). With no token configured every
# owner endpoint answers 503 (fail closed); a missing or wrong bearer answers 401.
#
# Prefer the FILE form in a service unit: the value then stays out of `systemctl show`, out
# of the process environment and out of every log line. The file must be mode 0600 and hold
# the token on one line; an empty or unreadable file resolves to "no token" (fail closed):
# LINUXDO_AI_OWNER_TOKEN_FILE=/home/young/.config/linuxdo-ai/owner-token
#
# Inline form - dev only, because the value becomes visible in the process environment:
# LINUXDO_AI_OWNER_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ CORS
# Exact allowlist of browser origins, comma separated and normalized to scheme://host:port.
# Wildcards, bare hosts and reflected origins are refused, and the response only ever echoes
# the exact request origin. Every frontend that calls this API must be listed explicitly -
# same-origin POSTs send an Origin header too, so the service's own origin belongs here.
#
# The deployed pair is the GitHub Pages frontend plus the public API origin:
# LINUXDO_AI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://youngzyl.github.io,https://tcstw.youngzyl.me:8443

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- deployment
# The systemd user unit does not read this file: it loads ~/.config/linuxdo-ai/service.env
# (mode 0600) instead, which sets the filter key as LINUXDO_AI_FILTER_API_KEY plus the
# LINUXDO_AI_FILTER_BASE_URL / LINUXDO_AI_FILTER_MODEL overrides, along with the owner-token
# path and the origin list above.
